  "answer": "## Known facts\n- **Deployment `wine-quality-api`**: 2/2 desired replicas ready and available, 0 unavailable (tool `list_workloads`).\n- **Pods**: both (`...-htjv9`, `...-zv5g9`) phase Running, ready, 0 restarts, no waiting reason or termination reason (tool `list_workloads`).\n- **Unhealthy pods check**: 2 pods checked, 0 unhealthy, 0 warning events (tool `find_unhealthy_pods`).\n- **Service `wine-quality-api`**: ClusterIP on port 80 → target port `http`, matching 2 pods, all 2 ready (tool `inspect_services`).\n- **Deployed version**: image `docker.io/library/wine-quality-api:model-v6`, model version **6**, rollout complete (tool `get_deployed_version`).\n- **Prediction drift** (60 predictions read from both pods since each started): no feature drifted beyond 0.5σ — largest shift is chlorides at −0.21σ; every feature flagged `drifted: false` (tool `check_prediction_drift`).\n\n## Uncertainties\n- Drift check covers **input** drift only, based on 60 logged predictions since each Pod started — a small sample and no window length reported. It cannot confirm live accuracy because it has no true labels (per the tool's own limitation).\n- The **positive-prediction rate is 0.283 live vs 0.189 in training** (~50% higher). This is an output/label-rate gap, not input drift, so it isn't flagged as drift — but it's a discrepancy worth watching; it could mean the model is predicting positives more often than it did on training data. It does not prove a fault, only that the live label distribution differs from training.\n- No tool result shows end‑to‑end request success/error rates or latency, so \"healthy\" here reflects readiness and stability, not measured prediction correctness.\n\n## Recommended actions\nNo action needed to keep the API running — it is ready, stable (no restarts) and serving model v6 with no input drift. If you want to close the remaining gap, I can pull recent pod logs (`get_pod_status_and_logs`) to look for request errors or latency, and/or dig into MLflow runs to compare whether model v6's quality gate passed and what data it was trained on.",
